1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,105
The Power set is the set of all subsets. For example, if

2
00:00:03,205 --> 00:00:06,482
we have the set {1,2,3} the power set is the following set.

3
00:00:06,666 --> 00:00:08,813
So, it contains the individual elements,

4
00:00:08,933 --> 00:00:10,296
the pairs of elements,

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,550
the whole set and the emptyset at the

6
00:00:12,650 --> 00:00:14,923
bottom, which is a subset of every set.

7
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,926
We may notice that there are 2 to the power of 3 or

8
00:00:18,026 --> 00:00:21,029
8 members in the power set of a set with three elements.

9
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:23,866
Since another way to look at the power set, is we

10
00:00:23,966 --> 00:00:27,649
consider each possibility in the procedure of going by each element

11
00:00:27,749 --> 00:00:29,851
in the set and either saying yes or no.

12
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:32,671
If we say yes to all elements, we get the whole set.

13
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,591
If we say no to each, we get the

14
00:00:34,691 --> 00:00:37,428
emptyset, and then we get everything in between.

15
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,204
We will now use this to define the so-called Von Neuman Hierarchy of

16
00:00:41,304 --> 00:00:44,526
sets V, which is often considered to be THE Universe of sets.

17
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:47,268
Again, we start with the empty set at the bottom, and

18
00:00:47,368 --> 00:00:50,351
then successively take the power set of the previous level.

19
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:52,941
So we get the set with the emptyset at the first level, then

20
00:00:53,041 --> 00:00:55,759
the emptyset plus the set with the emptyset at the second level,

21
00:00:55,866 --> 00:00:58,825
And so on. This seems tame and boring, but this is

22
00:00:58,925 --> 00:01:02,739
a hyper-exponential function, the size of each level is the size

23
00:01:02,839 --> 00:01:05,614
of the previous level raised to the power of 2.

24
00:01:05,933 --> 00:01:09,102
So, the third level has 16 elements, the fourth level

25
00:01:09,202 --> 00:01:12,124
has 65 Thousand, and the fifth level has way more

26
00:01:12,224 --> 00:01:14,714
sets than there are atoms in the Universe.

27
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:17,573
We can see that each level contains the next ordinal.

28
00:01:18,733 --> 00:01:21,812
We can repeat this procedure indefinitely, resulting

29
00:01:21,912 --> 00:01:24,197
in the structure which we call V_omega.

30
00:01:24,333 --> 00:01:26,651
We can then add in the following

31
00:01:26,751 --> 00:01:29,901
new axioms, to get the theory ZFC-INFINITY.

32
00:01:30,066 --> 00:01:32,497
These two axioms only make sense if we have infinite

33
00:01:32,597 --> 00:01:34,590
sets, so we don't need to worry about them.

34
00:01:37,466 --> 00:01:40,991
The replacement axiom just states that our Set theoretic Universe is

35
00:01:41,091 --> 00:01:44,509
closed under functions. Meaning that if we have a function defined

36
00:01:44,609 --> 00:01:46,587
on a set, then the range is also a set.

37
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:52,616
And this is the axiom of separation, which given some pre-existing set

38
00:01:52,716 --> 00:01:55,497
Y, allows us to separate out all of the sets in Y

39
00:01:55,597 --> 00:01:59,378
which satisfy a certain property. Where to get a bit technical, by

40
00:01:59,478 --> 00:02:03,024
property we mean a First order formula with one free variable.

41
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:07,236
For example, we can use the formula \exists x(x+x=y)

42
00:02:07,336 --> 00:02:11,601
to separate the even numbers from the natural numbers.

43
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:16,010
This formula is only true if we instantiate y with an even number.

44
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:19,162
Note, that the restriction that we are separating the elements

45
00:02:19,262 --> 00:02:22,274
from a pre-existing set is necessary to avoid paradoxes. Since,

46
00:02:22,374 --> 00:02:24,398
without it, we could define the set X to be

47
00:02:24,498 --> 00:02:26,966
the set of all sets which do not contain themselves.

48
00:02:27,133 --> 00:02:31,552
This is defined by a simple formula with one free variable, yet we get

49
00:02:31,652 --> 00:02:34,974
that X in X iff X not in X. Which is a contradiction.

50
00:02:35,066 --> 00:02:39,117
But anyways, if we stop the construction of our Universe here, we

51
00:02:39,217 --> 00:02:42,884
get a model of ZFC-Infinity, since we can show that each of

52
00:02:42,984 --> 00:02:47,035
these axioms hold true in this structure, yet each set is finite.

53
00:02:47,133 --> 00:02:49,938
However, this structure is logically equivalent to the

54
00:02:50,038 --> 00:02:53,328
number line with addition and multiplication described earlier.

55
00:02:53,466 --> 00:02:56,788
Meaning that both structures can be interpreted within the other.

56
00:02:56,933 --> 00:03:00,061
So, this tells us that if we want to go beyond simple

57
00:03:00,161 --> 00:03:04,507
elementary school math, we will need infinite sets. But infinite sets are

58
00:03:04,607 --> 00:03:08,405
confusing and cause issues when trying to formalize all of math.

